  "summary": "I've always been drawn to patterns, it’s what pulled me toward computer science, higher math, and eventually software engineering. There's something deeply satisfying about finding the cleanest, most elegant solution to a complex problem.\n\n Over the past 6+ years I've built full-stack web applications, developed enterprise automation pipelines using UiPath and Automation Anywhere, and shipped production software at companies like Dell Technologies, Synovus, and Intergraph (Hexagon). I hold a Master of Science in Software Engineering from Auburn University (4.0 GPA) and a BS in Computer Science, both from Auburn's Samuel Ginn College of Engineering.    \n\nWhat I enjoy most is the intersection of technology and process. That means figuring out not just how to build something, but why it should be built that way, and how it fits into the bigger picture of how people actually work.  Open to software engineering, automation, and workflow integration roles.\n\n\"Perfection is achieved, not when there is nothing more to add, but when there is nothing left to take away.\" — Antoine de Saint-Exupéry",
